This way you can  visualize the landmarks.

Output folders:
  • images/Train/landmarked/ — 📸 images overlaid with the 68 facial landmarks (red), if points/<name>.pts exists.
  • images/Train/landmarked_reduced/ — 📸 images overlaid with the reduced landmark set (blue), if points_reduced/<name>.pts exists.


4) 

Run:
python utils/segment_patches_morph.py 
python utils/segment_patches_fgnet.py
python utils/segment_patches_utkface.py
python utils/segment_patches_clap2016.py

What it does:
  • Analyzes preprocessed face images.
  • Assigns facial keypoints to a 6×6 grid of regular, overlapping patches.
  • Saves the results both as a CSV and as a visual image with patches and landmarks overlaid, under Train/images_segmented/.

Inputs:
Loads reduced landmarks from points_dir, e.g.:
  • MORPH → datasets/data/MORPH/points_reduced
  • FGNET → datasets/data/FGNET/points_reduced
  • UTKFace → datasets/data/UTKFace/points_reduced
  • CLAP2016 → datasets/data/CLAP2016/points_reduced


5) 
After that, run:

python main_morph.py
python main_fgnet.py
python main_utkface.py
python main_clap2016.py

These call graph_constructor_morph.py / graph_constructor_fgnet.py / graph_constructor_utkface.py / graph_constructor_clap2016.py to build the graph for each image and perform the following Stesp:

1️⃣ Load image + patch CSV — uses image_path, csv_path.
2️⃣ Build base graph + Random Walk refinement — construct_initial_graph.
3️⃣ Save graph_initial.pt, graph_rw.pt.
4️⃣ Apply Latent Relation Capturer (LRC) — LatentRelationCapturer.
5️⃣ Save LRC graphs — graph_lrc_*.pt (8 files).
6️⃣ Extract deep features with ResGCN — extract_deep_features.
7️⃣ Save deep_features.pt.

Outputs (per image)
	•	node_features.pt — 512-D visual embedding for each patch (node).
	•	edge_features.pt — (optional) mean embedding for connected pairs.
	•	graph_initial.pt — initial similarity-based graph.
	•	graph_rw.pt — graph after Random Walk.
	•	graph_lrc_*.pt — LRC-connected graphs via multi-head attention (8 files).
	•	deep_features.pt — final features from ResGCN.

✅ Conclusion
	•	✔ Yes, the system also generates patch/node embeddings.
	•	✔ They’re saved as node_features.pt inside the image’s folder.
	•	✔ Located under embeddings_morph, embeddings_FGNET, embeddings_utkface, or embeddings_clap2016.

