16)
Run:
python evaluate_rl_last15.py --dataset MORPH     # oppure FGNET / UTKFACE / CLAP2016
What it does:
	1.	Loads the last 15 checkpoints matching best_agent_*.pth from checkpoints/<DATASET>_clean514/.
	2.	Evaluates each one on the entire validation set, printing MAE, CS@5, ε-error (and decade accuracy if available).
	3.	Picks the best by MAE, saves a summary CSV, creates BEST_SELECTED.json, and copies the best model to best_agent_SELECTED.pth.
	4.	Compares the best RL model with the classifier baseline (decade accuracy + “soft” age from midpoint).
	5.	Generates artifacts for the best model: per-sample CSV, comparative table (CSV + PNG), confusion matrix, classification report, and a smoothed accuracy curve.

17)
Run:

python evaluate_rl_last15_x_mae.py --dataset MORPH  --epsilon-eval 0.65

This variant evaluates the last 15 RL checkpoints with an MAE-focused setup.
--epsilon-eval 0.65 sets the ε used at evaluation (e.g., for ε-greedy policy), and the script selects the best model by MAE, saving the usual summary artifacts (CSV, best checkpoint, etc.).


